---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProfileLinks from '../components/ProfileLinks.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
import { getPosts, fmtDate } from '../lib';
const posts = (await getPosts()).slice(0, 3);
---
<Base title={SITE.name}>
<main class="prof">
  <div class="top">
    <div>
      <h1 class="name"><b>Nihal</b> Vellaramkallingal Sulaiman</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Data analyst and BI developer · Niagara Falls, Ontario</p>
      <ProfileLinks />
    </div>
    {/* To use a photo: replace this div with <img class="photo" src="/assets/photo.jpg" alt="Nihal"> */}
    <div class="photo" aria-hidden="true">N</div>
  </div>

  <div class="bio">
    <p>I build end-to-end data work in Python and SQL: pipelines and star-schema warehouses, data-quality checks, dashboards that managers open every morning, and forecasts and schedules that save money. I hold a <b>Master's in Data Analytics</b> from the University of Niagara Falls Canada and an <b>MSc in Physics</b> (astrophysics, with a mathematics minor) from Cochin University of Science and Technology.</p>
    <p>Physics taught me to model a messy signal and check every number; analytics taught me to turn that into a decision someone can act on. I also know hotel operations from the floor, from over a year in hotel housekeeping in Niagara Falls. I am open to data analyst, BI developer and data science roles anywhere in Ontario.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>news</h2>
  <dl class="news">
    <dt>Nov 2026</dt><dd>Started a <a href="/blog/">blog</a> with write-ups of my projects and Kaggle work, and moved this site to nihalsulaiman.com.</dd>
    <dt>Nov 2026</dt><dd>Added an <a href="https://github.com/nihalunfc/hotel-business/tree/main/ai-workflow">AI workflow kit</a> to the Hospitality BI portfolio: safety rules for Claude Code on a live warehouse, an ETL triage method and a tested read-only SQL runner.</dd>
    <dt>Nov 2026</dt><dd>Currently in the top 10% of 4,346 on the public leaderboard of Kaggle's <i>Name That LLM</i> competition.</dd>
    <dt>Oct 2026</dt><dd>Graduated with a Master's in Data Analytics.</dd>
    <dt>Oct 2026</dt><dd>Launched the <a href="/hotel-business/">Hospitality BI portfolio</a>: a revenue command centre, a staff schedule builder and 12 hotel tools on a five-hotel sample group.</dd>
    <dt>Sep 2026</dt><dd>Built <a href="https://github.com/nihalunfc/GDGCHackathon2026">WARL</a>, a drone-swarm wildfire response with a live dashboard, at the GDG on Campus Build with AI hackathon.</dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>selected projects</h2>
  <div class="item">
    <div class="head"><h3><a href="/hotel-business/">Hospitality BI portfolio</a></h3><span class="when">2026</span></div>
    <p>A synthetic five-hotel group with about 640,000 bookings over four years, loaded into a star-schema warehouse with ten automated data-quality checks. The Revenue Command Centre shows occupancy, ADR, RevPAR, booking pace against last year, a back-tested demand forecast and demand lost on sold-out nights. The staff schedule builder turns forecast workload into shifts with integer programming and checks them against Ontario labour rules.</p>
    <div class="tags"><span class="tag">SQL</span><span class="tag">Python</span><span class="tag">Star schema</span><span class="tag">Forecasting</span><span class="tag">PuLP</span><span class="tag">Dashboards</span></div>
    <div class="more"><a href="/hotel-business/revenue.html">Revenue command centre</a><a href="/hotel-business/schedule.html">Schedule builder</a><a href="/hotel-business/tools/index.html">Hotel tools</a><a href="https://github.com/nihalunfc/hotel-business">Code</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="item">
    <div class="head"><h3><a href="/swarm/">Swarm intelligence</a></h3><span class="when">2026</span></div>
    <p>One engine in which many small agents each make their own decision and together act as a coordinated team, tested against today's rules on hotel equipment, grid batteries and wildfire drones.</p>
    <div class="tags"><span class="tag">Multi-agent RL</span><span class="tag">Optimisation</span><span class="tag">D3</span></div>
    <div class="more"><a href="/swarm/hotel/">Hotel operations</a><a href="/swarm/energy/">Grid batteries</a><a href="/swarm/wildfire/">Wildfire drones</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="item">
    <div class="head"><h3><a href="https://github.com/nihalunfc/GDGCHackathon2026">WARL: wildfire response with a drone swarm</a></h3><span class="when">2026</span></div>
    <p>A decentralised drone swarm trained with a PyTorch DQN to route to fire choke points, with a live map dashboard and a Gemini chatbot that explains the swarm's decisions.</p>
    <div class="tags"><span class="tag">PyTorch</span><span class="tag">Reinforcement learning</span><span class="tag">Leaflet</span><span class="tag">Gemini API</span></div>
    <div class="more"><a href="https://nihalunfc.github.io/GDGCHackathon2026/docs/">Demo</a><a href="https://github.com/nihalunfc/GDGCHackathon2026">Code</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="item">
    <div class="head"><h3><a href="/kaggle/">Kaggle competitions</a></h3><span class="when">2026</span></div>
    <p>Machine learning, deep learning and optimisation competitions, including LLM identification, mass-spectrometry structure identification and smart-building forecasting. I keep honest hold-out sets and report where a result came from.</p>
    <div class="tags"><span class="tag">XGBoost</span><span class="tag">LightGBM</span><span class="tag">PyTorch</span><span class="tag">Optuna</span></div>
    <div class="more"><a href="/kaggle/">Ranks and write-ups</a><a href="https://www.kaggle.com/vsnihal">Kaggle profile</a><a href="https://github.com/nihalunfc/kaggle">Code</a></div>
  </div>

  <h2>writing</h2>
  {posts.map((p) => (
    <div class="item">
      <div class="head"><h3><a href={`/blog/${p.id}/`}>{p.data.title}</a></h3><span class="when">{fmtDate(p.data.date)}</span></div>
      <p>{p.data.description}</p>
    </div>
  ))}
  <p class="more"><a href="/blog/">All posts</a><a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a></p>

  <h2>education</h2>
  <div class="item">
    <div class="head"><h3>Master's, Data Analytics</h3><span class="when">2026</span></div>
    <p class="where">University of Niagara Falls Canada, Ontario</p>
  </div>
  <div class="item">
    <div class="head"><h3>MSc Physics</h3><span class="when">2017 – 2019</span></div>
    <p class="where">Cochin University of Science and Technology, Kochi, India</p>
    <p>Astrophysics major, mathematics minor.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="item">
    <div class="head"><h3>BSc Physics</h3><span class="when">2013 – 2016</span></div>
    <p class="where">Government Victoria College, Palakkad (University of Calicut), India</p>
  </div>

  <p class="foot">More: <a href="/projects/">all projects</a> · <a href="/contact/">contact</a> · <a href="/sitemap/">site map</a> · <a href="/blog/">blog</a> · <a href="/now/">now</a> · <a href="/tools/">free tools</a> · <a href="/cv/">CV</a> · <a href="/about/">how I work</a></p>
</main>
</Base>
